==Battleground==
*1 [[Beefcake Cat (Enemy)|Beefcake Cat]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*10 [[Skelecat (Enemy)|Skelecats]] spawn after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Unicycle Cat (Enemy)|Unicycle Cat]] spawns after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*20 [[Gato Amigo (Enemy)|Gato Amigos]] spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Pastry Cat (Enemy)|Pastry Cat]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*3 [[Lollycat (Enemy)|Lollycats]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use the opening grace to save for [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]], and then start spamming [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]], and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] to protect her. Once you have enough money, start sending out [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cats]], as they will be your primary method to snipe the Lollycats. Keep up this process until you start to accrue enough wealth to afford [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cats]]. All of these Cats in tandem are going to aid in keeping Beefcake Cat at bay, although feel free to include [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] or [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] into your lineup if you have them (just don't go spamming them too much, else you'll go bankrupt).

Once the backline enemies bite the dust, cleaning up Beefcake Cat and Pastry Cat should be a breeze with all the sheer riches the supports drop.

